# command: osascript iterm-probe.applescript '<scratch>/iterm probe dir' (below), then the contents of each tab read back by AppleScript three seconds later, then the window closed
# date: 2026-11-19 22:40:59 UTC
# by: Opus 5.5 (implementer), Claude Code in iTerm2, on the operator's Mac, with the operator's leave in this session
## iTerm2 version: 3.7.8
## the script
on run argv
	set dir to item 1 of argv
	tell application "iTerm2"
		set w to (create window with default profile)
		tell current session of w to write text "cd -- '" & dir & "' && echo \"reopen probe tab 1: $PWD\""
		tell w
			set t to (create tab with default profile)
			tell current session of t to write text "echo 'reopen probe tab 2' && printf '%s\\n' \"it's quoted\""
		end tell
		return id of w
	end tell
end run
## osascript printed the new window's id (52376), took 0.93 s, and macOS asked nothing: osascript ran from a shell inside iTerm2, so iTerm2 drove itself
## the two tabs' contents, blank lines dropped, scratch path shortened
---- tab
